{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HPVA6cnPaQd6Z9HdCHxna3","type":"tool_result","content":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1643-`,\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1644-  },\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1645-  {\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts:1646:    slug: \"laksa-johor-guide-best-places-to-eat\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1647-    title: \"Laksa Johor Guide — Authentic Dish, Where to Eat, and What Makes It Unique (2026)\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1648-    excerpt:\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1649-      \"Deep-dive guide on Laksa Johor—a creamy coconut-based noodle dish unique to Johor. Covers history, what makes it different from other laksa variants, and the best stalls in JB.\",\n--\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1652-    author: \"Jay Lew\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1653-    readTime: \"6 min read\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1654-    tags: [\"food\", \"johor\", \"specialty-dish\", \"jb-guide\"],\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts:1655:    featuredImage: \"/images/blog/laksa-johor-guide.jpg\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1656-    content: `\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1657-<h2>What Is Laksa Johor?</h2>\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1658-<p><strong>Laksa Johor</strong> is a creamy coconut-based noodle soup unique to the state of Johor. Unlike laksa from other regions in Malaysia (Laksa Lemak from KL, Laksa Penang, Laksa Sarawak), Laksa Johor uses thick spaghetti noodles instead of rice noodles, giving it a distinctly different texture and mouthfeel. The broth is rich, aromatic, and infused with fish, coconut milk, and spices — making it one of the most indulgent noodle dishes in Malaysia.</p>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d69bad7-fd70-4f14-8ebe-891ae4eab84a","uuid":"2d59b83f-5a56-4cfc-8315-1d66a79cf203","timestamp":"2026-04-14T11:21:16.844Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1643-`,\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1644-  },\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1645-  {\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts:1646:    slug: \"laksa-johor-guide-best-places-to-eat\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1647-    title: \"Laksa Johor Guide — Authentic Dish, Where to Eat, and What Makes It Unique (2026)\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1648-    excerpt:\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1649-      \"Deep-dive guide on Laksa Johor—a creamy coconut-based noodle dish unique to Johor. Covers history, what makes it different from other laksa variants, and the best stalls in JB.\",\n--\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1652-    author: \"Jay Lew\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1653-    readTime: \"6 min read\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1654-    tags: [\"food\", \"johor\", \"specialty-dish\", \"jb-guide\"],\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts:1655:    featuredImage: \"/images/blog/laksa-johor-guide.jpg\",\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1656-    content: `\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1657-<h2>What Is Laksa Johor?</h2>\nC:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\Software Projects\\pelangi-website\\site\\src\\data\\blog\\posts.ts-1658-<p><strong>Laksa Johor</strong> is a creamy coconut-based noodle soup unique to the state of Johor. Unlike laksa from other regions in Malaysia (Laksa Lemak from KL, Laksa Penang, Laksa Sarawak), Laksa Johor uses thick spaghetti noodles instead of rice noodles, giving it a distinctly different texture and mouthfeel. The broth is rich, aromatic, and infused with fish, coconut milk, and spices — making it one of the most indulgent noodle dishes in Malaysia.</p>","numLines":15}}
